{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1177162-working-on-a-legacy-storm-dancers","id":1177162,"title":"Working on a Legacy: Storm-Dancers","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-01-18T21:14:57-08:00","id":1177162,"title":"Working on a Legacy: Storm-Dancers","content":"This is an idea that has been brewing in my head for a few days now, so I wanted to share my ideas thus far. There are a few attainments of which I am feeling uncertain, and the name could be more inspired. But, the idea is for a Legacy harnessing an ancient cosmic power that they can just barely control.<br /> <br /> Anyway:<br /> <br /> <b>Storm-Dancers</b><br /> <br /> Evidence of the Supernal is all around us; in the past, one merely needed to look to the skies, but nowadays even that isn't necessary. Electricity lies at the heart of magic--it was lightning that inspired humans to try striking stones together in order to create their own fire, lightning harnessed that allows our societies to flourish and progress, lightning within our very bodies that powers our brains and hearts. Lightning, like magic, is powerful, dynamic, creative, but also unpredictable and dangerous.<br /> <br /> The same adjectives also apply to the electro-shamans who revere this primal force of nature. In their scrapyards and copper-laden fields, occult laboratories and skyscraper rooftops, Storm-Dancers gaze upward and everywhere in awe of the sheer power coursing through everything, the true pulse of the living world found in cracklings and arcs. Wielding metal rods and purposefully-unhealed electrical scars, they scream in the language of the spirits to the ephemeral coursers willing to ally with mortals who treat them as fragments of gods. Where the Dancers tread, crazed and frenetic inspiration strikes the hapless, pushing them to sudden acts of creative greatness, if they can weather the storm, body and soul still intact.<br /> <br /> The Storm-Dancers claim to be one of those Legacies that have been around for most of forever, the reflection of a Supernal shamanic culture, or the result of humans across the world recognizing the divine power in a lightning strike. They might even be right, though investigators of history might note a spike in the Legacy's membership during the European Age of Enlightenment, which could mean any number of things, frankly. Mages of all Orders are accepted into the Storm-Dancers' ranks; the Silver Ladder, already accepting the truth of Lightning as Perfected Air, might turn frenzied storm-worship to a more priestly bent to encourage Sleepers to spiritual greatness, while a Libertine could see the potential in an ancient tradition still incredibly applicable to our modern, tech-driven days. In some lawless, storied places, the Storm-Dancers might even foster a cult to the General, but that may just be slander against a group so prone to nerve damage and ruined perms, so attractive to Nameless, Solitaries, and Apostates.<br /> <br /> <b>Parentage:</b> Thyrsus<br /> <br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Forces 2, Athletics 2, one of the following skills at 2 dots: Crafts, Expression, Intimidation, Occult, Persuasion, Science, Survival<br /> <br /> <b>Initiation: </b>Shamanic mysteries are lived experiences. In the case of Storm-Dancers, this means a prospective member has to feel the pulse of lightning within her--in other words, she has to electrocute herself. She is brought to a place lightning is likely to strike, she is properly equipped to draw the force to her, and she waits. The other members usually employ magic to ensure the ordeal isn't fatal and, considering Legacy's Path, statistically speaking at least one witness is bound to be proficient in healing spells.<br /> <br /> <b>Organization:</b> Storm-Dancers don't have any formal hierarchy. Local pecking orders based on age, power, and charisma sometimes form, but these can break apart just as easily as they coalesce. Those who have been struck by lightning more than others are generally given a measure of respect, touched as they are by a primal force.<br /> <br /> <b>Theory:</b> Electricity is in essence the Fallen version of Supernal magic. It powers the modern world and can kill without warning, and so should be respected and even venerated. Spirits of electrical forces tend to be fickle and temperamental and need to be appeased lest they run amok.<br /> <br /> <b>Ruling Arcanum:</b> Forces<br /> <br /> <b>Yantras:</b> Exposed wiring (+1), Lightning rods (+1), Electrocution (+2), Lightning strikes (+2), Fetishes bound with electricity spirits (+1 or +2 depending on Rank)<br /> <br /> <b>Oblations:</b> Standing out in a lightning storm, building an electrical device, performing chiminage for electricity spirits, meditating in an electrically-charged space<br /> <br /> <b>Attainments<br /> <br /> First (Initiation): </b>The Storm-Dancer can use Influence Electricity as an instant action, turning the lightning inside technology to her will.<br /> <br /> <b>Optional (Spirit 1):</b> The mage's very essence is attuned to the pulse of the storm. Add the Storm-Dancer's dots in Spirit to rolls to interact with electricity spirits.<br /> <br /> <b>Second (Athletics 3): </b>The mage can use Insulation as an instant action; she still feels pain from electricity, but can confidently grasp sources of power without fear of sudden death.<br /> <br /> <b>Optional (Spirit 2): </b>The mage can harness the power of electrical inspiration. This Attainment can only be used either in an area or an a subject with either the Resonant or Open Condition, keyed to electricity. After a scene-long ritual in which the Storm-Dancer coaxes spirits of lightning to provide aid, the subject adds the mage's Spirit dots to his next roll to Build Equipment (of any type).<br /> <br /> <b>Third (Forces 3, second skill 3):</b> In the heart of a storm, the mage can conjure glowing orbs to draw down the power of the sky. This replicates the spell Call Lightning, cast as an instant action.<br /> <br /> <b>Optional (Spirit 3):</b> The Storm-Dancer unlocks the ability to alter the pulse of the world so that her gods have more sway. She can use Opener of the Way as an instant action with advanced duration, though only for electricity-keyed resonance. However, she can also use this Attainment to add the Resonant (Electricity) Condition to a place that does not currently possess it.<br /> <br /> <b>Fourth (Forces 4, third skill 3):</b> The Storm-Dancer masters the ability to command the power of the heavens. This Attainment imitates the spell Control Electricity, with Reach assigned to instant casting, sensory range, and advanced scale.<br /> <br /> <b>Optional (Spirit 4):</b> A Storm-Dancer who is an Adept of Spirit can bind a willing (and not necessarily hibernating) electro-spirit to an object as per the spell Craft Fetish, requiring a scene-long ritual, with Reach applied for advanced duration.<br /> <br /> <b>Fifth (Forces 5, fourth skill 3):</b> At the zenith of her power, the Storm-Dancer can call forth a wild surge of energy anywhere. After a scene-long ritual of dancing, setting up lightning rods, and invocations to the forces of nature, the mage can use Adverse Weather, with Reach applied for advanced duration. This Attainment can only be used to create an electrical storm. In exchange for this limitation, the shaman is given a level of dynamism rarely seen elsewhere; while within the confines of the conjured storm, the Storm-Dancer gains an additional free Reach to use as she wishes for any of her lesser Attainments.<br /> <br /> <b>Optional (Spirit 5):</b> The Storm-Dancer's electrical powers affect the Gauntlet as well. When unleashing her ultimate Attainment, the mage may spend a point of Mana to make the area affected by the storm a Locus (with Resonance attuned to electricity, of course). The Locus dissipates at the same moment as the summoned lightning storm.<br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> <b>Insulation (Forces 2)<br /> Practice:</b> Shielding<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Athletics, Science, Survival<br /> <br /> The mage wards the subject against electricity. For the spell's Duration, the subject takes no damage from mundane electrical sources. He is not immune to the secondary effects of electricity, however. Supernatural lightning attacks provoke a Clash of Wills.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The subject is also immune to the secondary effects of electrical damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1423,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","user":"espritdecalmar","date":". 01-22-2018, 11:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-19T07:57:36-08:00","id":1177283,"title":"","content":"The first and second attainments are touch range only?<br /> <br /> The third and fourth attainments are kind of repetitive being just directed energy attacks. Maybe make the second or third attainment a Shielding effect so you can\u2019t be electrocuted while under its effects?<br /> <br /> Other than that looks good, though I think you should point out where all Reach is spent on each attainment to make it easier to judge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-19T08:05:06-08:00","id":1177287,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1177162-working-on-a-legacy-storm-dancers?p=1177283#post1177283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The first and second attainments are touch range only?<br /> <br /> The third and fourth attainments are kind of repetitive being just directed energy attacks. Maybe make the second or third attainment a Shielding effect so you can\u2019t be electrocuted while under its effects?<br /> <br /> Other than that looks good, though I think you should point out where all Reach is spent on each attainment to make it easier to judge.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for your feedback. Yes, the first and second Attainments are both touch-range. I was considering a Shielding effect, but that also seems to be covered by Control Electricity (you can direct electricity away from someone to reduce damage by the spell's Potency).<br /> <br /> Maybe I could change the Thunderbolt Attainment into a modified Transform Energy. I'll think that over.<br /> <br /> Reach is spent as follows:<br /> <br /> 1: Instant Casting. (Optional: An always-on effect that's essentially a limited version of a homebrew Spirit Compelling spell I call &quot;Align Essence.&quot;)<br /> <br /> 2: Instant Casting. (Optional: Special.)<br /> <br /> 3: Instant Casting. (Optional: Instant Casting &amp; Advanced Duration, plus a slightly expanded ability to make up for the Attainment's limited breadth.)<br /> <br /> 4: Instant Casting. (Optional: Advanced Duration.)<br /> <br /> 5: Advanced Duration, Limited breadth, Special effect. (Optional: A specialized form of Create Locus.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1423,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","user":"espritdecalmar","date":". 01-19-2018, 11:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-19T08:38:52-08:00","id":1177308,"title":"","content":"Maximum Potency for the Control Electricity attainment if you leave it as Duration Primary will be Potency 2, and bade electricity damage is 8 Bashing. So you\u2019d still experience a pretty bad shock.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-19T08:50:16-08:00","id":1177311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1177162-working-on-a-legacy-storm-dancers?p=1177308#post1177308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maximum Potency for the Control Electricity attainment if you leave it as Duration Primary will be Potency 2, and bade electricity damage is 8 Bashing. So you\u2019d still experience a pretty bad shock.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, that is true. I feel like a complete Shielding effect is a little at odds with the theme I'm going for with this Legacy, but here's an idea:<br /> <br /> The Fourth Attainment is replaced by Control Electricity, with Reach assigned to Instant Casting, Advanced Scale, and Sensory Range. This means (if I'm understanding everything correctly) that when first acquired, the Attainment lasts for 5 turns, has a Potency of 3, and affects up to 5 subjects or everything within the space of a large house.<br /> <br /> The Second Attainment is replaced by a special effect: All electricity damage is reduced by the Storm-Dancer's Forces dots. Lightning can still hurt them, but it greatly increases their odds of survival.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1423,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","user":"espritdecalmar","date":". 01-19-2018, 11:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-19T08:58:21-08:00","id":1177313,"title":"","content":"They\u2019ve already survived being struck by lightning once, is there a reason they wouldn\u2019t want to be immune to the adverse effects when it happens again? Does being hurt when struck by lightning benefit them somehow?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-19T09:16:53-08:00","id":1177319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1177162-working-on-a-legacy-storm-dancers?p=1177313#post1177313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They\u2019ve already survived being struck by lightning once, is there a reason they wouldn\u2019t want to be immune to the adverse effects when it happens again? Does being hurt when struck by lightning benefit them somehow?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not mechanically at the moment (although I've considered adding to the prerequisites for each Attainment an additional bout of electrocution). It's more a thematic thing: People exposing themselves to a dangerous source of power and welcoming the pain it brings, because enlightenment can only come through direct experience. Also, the spirits they work with might be offended if they protect themselves too tightly against their essence. Those are just my initial thoughts, however; it's quite possible that that might make them less fun to play, which obviously is counterproductive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-19T09:19:41-08:00","id":1177322,"title":"","content":"I mean, there\u2019s nothing to say they can\u2019t still feel the pain of being electrocuted, just that they aren\u2019t incapacitated or injured by it, right? That kind of insulation means they could hurl themselves into their source of inspiration again and again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-22T08:07:57-08:00","id":1178076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1177162-working-on-a-legacy-storm-dancers?p=1177322#post1177322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, there\u2019s nothing to say they can\u2019t still feel the pain of being electrocuted, just that they aren\u2019t incapacitated or injured by it, right? That kind of insulation means they could hurl themselves into their source of inspiration again and again.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's fair. Okay, I think the 2nd Attainment then will be immunity to mundane electrical damage, and an automatic Clash against supernatural electricity, though the mage still has to roll to escape from a continuous power source.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}